## 9.CONCLUSION
The Bank Account Management System using Stack and Queue with Dynamic Implementation was developed using C++. The project demonstrates how linked nodes and dynamic memory allocation can be used to manage banking-related records.
The Stack implements the LIFO principle and supports push, pop, peek, and display operations. The Queue implements the FIFO principle and supports enqueue, dequeue, front, and display operations.
Through this project, the concepts of pointers, linked nodes, dynamic memory allocation, insertion, deletion, and memory deallocation are demonstrated. The project also illustrates how different data structures can be selected according to the requirements of a problem.
